## Required manuscript-level conclusion

The coherent claim should be:

> A common realized Bregman divergence quantifies perturbation-induced response change. Its FBA and time-course realizations are finite response divergences. The geometric quantity \(\kappa^{\mathrm{geo}}\) is a local two-directional curvature operator derived from that divergence. Under a regularized FBA embedding and an explicitly constructed sensitivity transport, a four-condition FBA plaquette estimator converges to \(\kappa^{\mathrm{geo}}\).

If the empirical design cannot be expanded to paired perturbations, the paper should make the weaker but honest claim:

> The FBA and transcriptomic analyses validate the response-divergence layer, not the geometric curvature theorem.

That is the repaired object and the precise limit of the unification. The existing three quantities should not continue to share the bare name \(\kappa_V\).